  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure over the area will keep conditions dry through at\nleast the middle of next week. Northwesterly flow will lead to \nseasonably cool conditions this afternoon with highs in the 50s \nalong with less wind in comparison to yesterday. As trick- or- \ntreating time starts to roll around early this evening, \ntemperatures will likely range from the upper 40s to the mid 50s\nby late afternoon, and fall into the 40s areawide just after \nsunset. With light winds and high pressure overhead it will be \nchillier overnight with lows in the mid 20s to the mid 30s. \n\nAs the center high starts to shift slowly east tomorrow, the \nflow will gradually turn more westerly aloft and temperatures \nmoderate a bit with highs in the upper 50s to lower 60s. A \nwarming trend continues through mid-week, with upper- level \nridging building in aloft and the flow becoming more south- \nsouthwesterly. Afternoon highs early next week will be running \nwell above average in the 60s with some valley locations even \nmaking a run at 70 degrees Tuesday and Wednesday. The next \nopportunity for more meaningful rainfall looks to be later \nWednesday night into Thursday as a frontal boundary approaches.",
